{
  "rationale": "The plant automata model the robot's motion and perception capabilities, separating motion commands from sensor outcomes. The specification automata enforce safe, efficient exploration: random_walk is preferred in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and obstacle events trigger conservative, directed recovery (turns or, as a last resort, a full scan). The supervisor never allows forward or random_walk when an obstacle is detected in front, and always returns to exploration as soon as the path is clear.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for motion and perception: G1 models motion commands, G2 models sensor outcomes.",
    "Specification E1 encodes the exploration and recovery policy, ensuring safe transitions and maximizing coverage while avoiding collisions."
  ],
